# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this the context is ~1.8GB against ~1.5MB of tracked source, and
# both Dockerfiles copy a directory wholesale (`COPY backend/ .`,
# `COPY frontend/ .`). That puts host build artefacts inside the image:
#
#   * backend/.venv        host-built wheels, shadowing the image's own install
#   * backend/model_store  trained artefacts whose checksums will not match the
#                          registry of whatever database the image is deployed
#                          against -- predictions then fail closed with a
#                          checksum mismatch
#   * frontend/node_modules  copied AFTER the deps stage, so it overwrites the
#                          `npm ci` result; on a non-Linux dev machine that
#                          puts the wrong platform's binaries in the image
#
# Keep this list ahead of anything that writes into the working tree.

.git
.gitignore
.github

# Virtualenvs and package trees -- rebuilt inside the image.
**/.venv
**/venv
**/node_modules

# Build output -- regenerated by the image build.
**/.next
**/dist
**/build

# Trained model artefacts belong to the runtime registry, never the image.
**/model_store

# Python and test droppings.
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache
**/.mypy_cache
**/.ruff_cache
**/.coverage
**/coverage.xml
**/htmlcov

# Local configuration and secrets. .env.example is the documented template and
# is deliberately kept.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Editor and OS noise.
**/.DS_Store
**/.idea
**/.vscode
**/*.swp

# Claude Code session tooling -- not part of the runtime image.
.claude
